00:06:35.854 --> 00:06:38.925
And now back to the story.

00:06:38.925 --> 00:06:41.925
(suspenseful music)

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.670
Okay, so you have this sort
of bizarre border dispute

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.510
between the US and Canada.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.600
But there aren't any natural resources

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:54.260
for anyone to actually care about this.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.120
But that quickly starts to change.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.242
As I drove North into New England,

00:06:58.242 --> 00:07:01.280
I became familiar with a natural resource

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.420
that is actually very valuable.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:06.350
And that would turn this
rocky lighthouse Island

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:08.810
into an actual conflict.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:11.175
And that resource looks like this.

00:07:11.175 --> 00:07:13.433
(bright music)

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.957
- [Man Two] This is lobster meat.

00:07:14.957 --> 00:07:17.450
It comes from a lobster that lives

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.029
at the bottom of the ocean and
the people catch around here

00:07:20.029 --> 00:07:21.633
and bring to my roll.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.780
- Lobstering is a big deal in Maine,

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:29.200
like a 500 million dollar big deal.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.410
It is the number one export
of the state and Maine,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.550
takes in more lobster than any other state

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.510
in the United States.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.480
And now surprisingly, it
is a big deal in Canada

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:40.970
who also has a giant lobster industry.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:44.000
This Grey Zone, the disputed
territory in the ocean

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.507
straddles the fishing zones
between the two countries.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:53.530
So right now, this is really
the crux of the conflict.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.886
You have a growing lobster
industry on both sides with

00:07:56.886 --> 00:07:59.900
independent Lobstermen trying
to maximize their catch

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:01.750
and going into the Grey Zone.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:04.150
The problem is that Canada
and the United States

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.520
have different rules
and regulations around

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.410
when you can fish, how much you can fish.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.140
But when they get into the Grey Zone,

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.100
a lot of that sort of goes out the window

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.450
and it leads to some major conflict,

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:17.330
some deep resentment
between the Lobstermen and

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.320
overfishing of this delicate Ecosystem.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.510
- [Narrator] We've had people shot over

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:24.870
lobster fishing complex, you know, and

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.230
significant violence over lobster fishing.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.860
- So I guess the big question is,

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:34.770
who actually owns this water?
Who has the more legit claim?

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:38.410
At the heart of the Canadian
claim is this light house.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.450
This light house was built
by the British in the 1800s.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.060
But the Canadians inherited it

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:45.910
and they've occupied it ever since.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.740
When you're disputing
over who owns what land

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:50.160
having physical
infrastructure on that land

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.397
is a pretty decent claim.

00:08:52.397 --> 00:08:55.140
And even though light houses
have become totally automated,

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.440
meaning they don't need
people to run them,

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.830
the Canadian Military has insisted on

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:02.550
keeping a person there 24 seven.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:05.030
They will helicopter out
someone and their family

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:07.990
to man this lighthouse at all times

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:09.960
to make sure that there are people there.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.460
Not because anyone needs to be
there to run the lighthouse,

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:15.030
but solely because they
want to beef up their claim

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:18.310
that this island and the
surrounding water is theirs.

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:20.790
If you want to see a glimpse into the day

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.430
of the life of the person
who unnecessarily mans

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.640
this random light house on a tiny island,

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.710
there's a really
beautifully shot short film

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.030
by a channel called "Jungles in Paris."

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:33.045
Which gives you an idea
of what this life is like.

00:09:33.045 --> 00:09:34.008
- [Light House Keeper]
Instead of being the keeper

00:09:34.008 --> 00:09:35.550
of the light house here you more of

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.270
the keeper of the island.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:41.460
- Meanwhile, the US basically
says all of this is bogus.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:43.150
That the island is rightfully theirs,

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.390
the fishery around the
island is rightfully theirs,

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:50.300
it has been since 1782
and they do not recognize

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:53.410
any sovereignty of Canada on this island.

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:57.400
The local fishermen and
population in Maine also are very

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.820
vehemently attached to the
US claims on this island.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.760
There was this guy, his
name was Barnabas what?

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:04.954
Bartnad, Barnabas?

00:10:04.954 --> 00:10:05.978
- Barna Norton.
- Barna Norton.

00:10:05.978 --> 00:10:07.040
- Barna.
- Barna.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.040
- Barna Norton.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.300
who would show up every year on the island

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:14.160
with an American flag
to plant it to assert

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.590
the sovereignty of the United States.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.190
- [Barna] So again, in front of this sign,

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:19.973
I declare this island
belongs to United States.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:24.500
- And just remember,
for the people in Maine,

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.630
this is not about Geopolitics.

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.460
This is about their livelihood,

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:32.180
the future of their livelihood
of their number one export

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:35.300
a huge part of their
lifestyle and their economy.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:39.070
And it's the locals who are
the most active in this fight.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:43.120
The US government, from a Federal
or State Department level,

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.010
kind of doesn't really
care most of the time.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:48.660
And meanwhile, while all of
this lobster drama is happening,

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.500
you have boats from both
countries bringing tourists

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.913
onto the islands to look at Puffins.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.840
So let's just get up to
speed see where we're at.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.300
We're talking about these
vaguely worded treaties that lead

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.940
to a territorial dispute that
no one really cared about

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:08.320
until they did because of lobsters.

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:11.360
And then Canada put a
person in this lighthouse

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.200
even though this lighthouse
didn't need a person

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.240
and then there's puffins.

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:17.130
Can you see now I'm
like way into the story?

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:20.485
Okay, so now let's talk
about Donald J. Trump.

00:11:20.485 --> 00:11:22.350
(sighs)

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:23.630
I know, okay.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:27.490
It turns out that this obscure,
small scale border dispute

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:30.070
is like click bait for Donald Trump.

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:30.903
I mean, think about it.

00:11:30.903 --> 00:11:33.630
This is a valuable American industry

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.510
that is being threatened
by outsiders coming in

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:39.060
and stealing our goods.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:40.920
It's just like, just perfect for him.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.650
This is an opportunity
to show American power.

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.940
- The Canadian government
is investigating reports.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:48.470
Canadian boats have been
approached and question

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.900
by US border patrol agents
at the Gulf of Maine.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:53.190
The US officials claim
they were looking for,

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.890
illegal immigrants and the
border officials have stopped

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:58.290
at least 10 fishing boats
in the past two weeks.

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:01.320
- So in 2018, the Trump
administration sends out

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.700
Border Patrol into the Grey Zone to stop

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.780
Canadian Lobstermen and interrogate them.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.770
They stopped 10 different
crews and asked them

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:12.600
about drugs and immigration.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.010
It's just like, come on dude.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.560
It was such a Trump thing to do.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.370
It wasn't like let's have some overtures

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.000
for some diplomatic conversations about

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.780
how we can actually resolve
this border dispute peacefully.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.840
It was like, send in the Border
Patrol and intimidate them

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.350
and show them how strong we are.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:27.806
- What's going on over here?

00:12:27.806 --> 00:12:29.630
- [Commentator] Hey look at this,

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:31.561
Donald Trump, Donald Trump.

00:12:31.561 --> 00:12:33.478
(crowd cheering)

00:12:33.478 --> 00:12:37.090
- [Commentator Two] The hostile
takeover of Donald Trump.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.610
- So fast forward to today.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:42.140
It's 2020 and we're in an election year.

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:44.680
And when I say that the
US government doesn't care

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.730
about this border dispute,
the caveat to that

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.436
is during an election
year, suddenly they care.

00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:53.019
(upbeat music)

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:57.730
Because the people of
Mainecare and the people

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:01.370
of Maine who care also vote
and you get the picture here.

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:04.580
The Senator from Maine,
Susan Collins wrote a letter

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:05.900
to the Trump administration.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:06.820
And she was like,

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.520
Thanks so much for sending your like

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:11.518
badass Border Patrol out to
intimidate the Canadians.

00:13:11.518 --> 00:13:15.300
It didn't really do anything,
can we actually find a useful,

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:18.100
enduring solution to this conflict,

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.620
through, you know diplomacy?

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:22.050
She mentioned that the
Grey Zone is home to this

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.000
valuable part of the
livelihood of people in Maine

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.360
and asked the administration
to actually do something.

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:32.300
Meanwhile, Trump has shown a
strange interest in this issue.

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:34.870
He actually went to Maine
and hosted this round table

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.080
with a bunch of people
from the fishing industry.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.207
And he brought up the Grey Zone.

00:13:39.207 --> 00:13:41.580
- How did you let that, how
do they let that happen?

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:43.020
- [Man] Obama just used it.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.497
- That was President Obama.
Thank you very much.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:51.780
- So this meeting ended
up being Trump going up

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:55.150
to basically rally these
people and be pissed off

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.710
with them about how
they're being screwed out

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:57.950
of their lobster.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.360
- You got to be kidding.
Is that right?

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:01.478
- [Man] That's correct, Sir.

00:14:01.478 --> 00:14:03.590
- So they just closed it
they said you can't fish.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.690
But let me guess other countries do right?

00:14:07.226 --> 00:14:08.850
Yeah, they do.

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:10.950
- And then of course, he
followed his standard script

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.027
and basically mentioned how great is.

00:14:13.027 --> 00:14:14.963
- [Donald Trump] You
so lucky I'm president,

00:14:14.963 --> 00:14:16.112
you are so lucky.

00:14:16.112 --> 00:14:18.740
I don't even know you
and you are so lucky.

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:21.950
- So the upshot here is
that Canada cares a lot more

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:24.810
about this sovereignty claim
than the United States.

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:27.130
Unless it's an election
year, in which case,

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.820
US politicians will do some little things

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:32.760
to curry favor among Lobstermen.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.480
The US doesn't really
care that much about this,

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.910
not nearly as much as
Canada does who actually

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:41.500
uses their military
resources to man this island.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:44.860
This dispute and the status
quo is likely to stay

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.310
sort of as it is unless of course,

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:52.310
they discover a legitimately
valuable resource like oil

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:54.340
or some other very valuable thing.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:57.100
If that were to happen I think the US

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.950
from like a foreign policy
standpoint would step up

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.650
to the plate and actually wage this war.

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:05.400
So for now, the lighthouse will continue

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:08.410
to be unnecessarily manned by a Canadian.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:11.570
The Lobstermen will keep
fighting and overfishing

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:14.004
in the Grey Zone and
boats from both countries

00:15:14.004 --> 00:15:16.621
will continue to cut out loads of tourists

00:15:16.621 --> 00:15:19.019
to take pictures of Puffins.

00:15:19.019 --> 00:15:21.602
(bright music)

